    {
        id hardening
        title "Post-review hardening: fix what the adversarial reviews found"
        kind @fix
        children (
            {
                id hd-topic-classes
                title "One topic-class scheme: registry-served span classes; revive the three inert topics"
                kind @fix
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T21:49:43.434494Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "Coherence H1: frontend derives hit class as \"teaksta-\"+registry name (teaksta-web markup.rs:115), but Conjunctions/NegVerbs/InfiniteVerbs emit teaksta-conjunction (+teaksta-CC/CS), teaksta-ConNeg, teaksta-InfiniteVerb (conjunction.rs:104, con_neg.rs:22, infinite_verb.rs:21) — those three topics are inert in every mode. Fix: make the registry the single source (serve span_class per activity in /api/activities; frontend uses the served class), or rename the three enhancer constants to match directory names. Also: regenerate live fixtures (they still carry WERTi-span ids), fix the residue guards (ui/mod.rs:90 greps WERTiServlet, exercise_modes.rs:131 greps wertiview — neither matches actual residue), and add at least one non-Substantive fixture family so the seam is tested. Related M12: SPAN_ID_PREFIX const exists unused while five sites hand-roll the literal."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id hd-click-decoys
                title "Click-mode decoys: settle the dead TokenEnhancer path against the Java reference"
                kind @fix
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T21:49:53.144664Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "Coherence H2: TokenEnhancer (first stage of every shipped postprocessor) is dead two ways — Vislcg3Annotator empties cas.tokens (vislcg3.rs:210-226) before it runs, and nothing writes Token.tag/.lemma (tokenizer.rs:235 sets only begin/end). So teaksta-hit and relevant:false are never produced, the frontend GENERIC_HIT_CLASS fallback (markup.rs:121) never fires, and click mode has zero decoys — every clickable word is correct; exercise_modes.rs:120 asserts the degenerate state. Check sme/ Java reference: did legacy click actually have decoys (did anything populate tag/lemma there)? If yes, resurrect the pass over cg_tokens; if legacy was equally broken, excise TokenEnhancer + the relevant flag + html_utils.rs:349-358's stated intent honestly and give click real decoys from the cg data by design. Also panic-audit finding 4: token.rs:87 calls the unchecked Document::covered_text (types.rs:124) — kept safe only by the accidental emptiness; whatever resurrection happens must use the checked form."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id hd-cache
                title "Analysis-cache safety: recover from bad cache files, validate offsets, keyed stable cache key"
                kind @fix
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T21:50:01.332393Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "Coherence H3 + panic 4/7 + cache-poisoning. (1) page_handler.rs:123-133: cache read failure logs, skips both pipelines, serves the empty PageMap as 200, and never rewrites the file — fall through to re-analysis and overwrite on parse failure. (2) read_xmi (page_handler.rs:53) deserializes offsets with no validation; make Document::covered_text (types.rs:124) checked (the safe helper already exists at vislcg3.rs:58) and validate spans against text at the deserialization edge — any types.rs change or offset-semantics drift currently becomes a repeatable per-page failure. (3) api.rs:444-448 cache key: DefaultHasher (unstable across releases, unkeyed SipHash — offline-collidable, attacker controls both sides via POST html) over URL only — ignores activity and mode, so an analysis for one topic is reused for another. Use a keyed/stable hash and include activity+mode in the key. Also panic 13: write_xmi failure silently skips the postprocessor (page_handler.rs:136-144) — surface it."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id hd-request-limits
                title "Request hardening: body size limits and CatchPanic across all routes"
                kind @fix
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T21:50:07.389231Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "Panic-audit CRITICAL 1: /api/enhance has no SizeLimit (api.rs:168-177 — only /api/upload does); poem's Json extractor buffers unbounded, then serde + Html::parse_document copy it twice more, so one chunked POST streaming an endless html field OOMs the process. Add SizeLimit to the enhance routes (and a sane cap on SpanRequest.html). Panic 9: no CatchPanic middleware — an async-side panic resets the connection with no 500 and no structured log; add poem's CatchPanic at the router root (main.rs:42). Cheap, purely additive node — good first pick."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T23:10:58.397604Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id hd-morpho
                title "Un-wedge morpho: lock scope, poison recovery, retryable generator init, typed errors"
                kind @fix
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T21:50:16.562308Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "Panic-audit HIGH 2+3, idiom M41/M42, all in morpho.rs. (1) :71-101 holds the handles mutex across the whole block_on and converts poisoning into a permanent error — one panic inside divvun-runtime/cg3/hfst wedges every enhance+upload until restart. Recover with into_inner() (AppState::analysis_lock at api.rs:138 already does) and drop/narrow the guard so a pipeline panic can't poison the registry. (2) :227-254 OnceLock<Result<...>> caches a failed generator load as the initialized value — first mc/cloze request with a bad TEAKSTA_GENERATOR bricks generation for the process even after the operator fixes it; only store on success (Mutex<Option<...>> or equivalent retry). (3) M41 :259-271 lookup_surfaces returns empty Vec for both transducer failure and unknown word, so generate emits input+? for real errors — return Result. (4) M42: the String error in the OnceLock is stringly typed and rebuilt context-free per call — thiserror enum or Arc<anyhow::Error>. Corrupt-file parsing runs inside hfst-rs which has unreachable!/expect sites — contained by spawn_blocking, but the retry fix is what makes it survivable."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T22:39:07.831779Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id hd-fetch
                title "Fetch hardening: shared client, file: confinement, SSRF policy, encoded file URLs"
                kind @fix
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T21:50:25.644788Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "Security triad + idiom H9/H10, all on the page-fetch path. (1) api.rs:455-459: file: scheme reads any local path — GET /api/enhance?url=file:///etc/passwd works; confine to config.upload_keep_dir/upload_temp_dir after canonicalization. (2) SSRF: no scheme/host policy on http(s), and page_url (api.rs:431-439) prepends http:// to bare hosts; block link-local/metadata/private ranges (the service fetches arbitrary public pages by design, so the policy is deny-private, not allowlist). (3) Idiom H9 / panic 8: fresh reqwest::blocking::Client per fetch (api.rs:461-463) — each spawns a dedicated OS thread + runtime; ~512 tarpit URLs with FETCH_TIMEOUT=20s exhaust the blocking pool and starve /api/upload. One static LazyLock client with the timeout baked in, plus a concurrency cap on the fetch path. (4) Idiom H10: file: URLs built by format!(\"file://{path}\") with no percent-encoding (upload.rs:245, activity_configuration.rs:100-105) and round-tripped through Url::parse at api.rs:438 — a deployment path with a space breaks all uploads; use Url::from_file_path."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id hd-config
                title "Config coherence: TEAKSTA_CLASSPATH into Config, complete startup warnings"
                kind @fix
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-10T21:50:32.872414Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "Coherence M4: TEAKSTA_CLASSPATH is a bare literal in activity_configuration.rs:60 — not a Config field (context.rs owns the other six *_ENV consts), absent from context.rs:113-120's env save/restore and from main.rs:24-28's startup warnings. It resolves into a OnceLock on first read, so set_classpath_root (:53, sole caller pipeline_models.rs:61) silently loses to whoever read first and returns a bool nobody checks. Move it into Config, make the classpath root flow from Config instead of a process global, and make the startup warnings cover the full env surface. Also coherence M9 while in here: Document.language is a pipeline registry key always \"en\" in production (api.rs:39) while every unit test says \"sme\" — either rename the field for what it is or make runtime and tests agree."
                    }
                )
            }

