                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "Operator decision (2026-09-10): wire the UI to the span endpoint rather than contract-only or deletion. Today fetch_spans/SpanRequest/parse_spans/EnhancedSpans (teaksta-web api.rs:99-133) have zero production callers (coherence M1, idiom M45); the UI fetches the whole enhanced page and re-parses with the 816-line markup.rs lexer. Target shape: exercise modes fetch the raw page plus POST /api/enhance span map and splice client-side, shrinking the lexer's role to the raw page. Both sides' types already match exactly (verified in review — SpanRequest one-of html/url invariant, attribute vocabulary character-for-character). Note the span map alone can't render a page: keep the page fetch for document context, the span map keys by position. PAGE_SPAN_CLASS \"teaksta-page\" (enhancer_utils.rs:12) currently has no consumer anywhere and no CSS — the wiring should either consume or drop it. Depends on hd-topic-classes (class vocabulary single-sourced first) and hd-click-decoys (relevant/hit semantics settled first so the span map carries them)."
